---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Check every addon of the target series against older series (maintainer mode): portable pull requests and false positives (migration commits, repo-wide changes, translations)

Usage: odx port sweep [OPTIONS] --to <SERIES> --from <SERIES>

Options:
      --to <SERIES>
          Target series

      --from <SERIES>
          Source series, comma-separated or repeated

      --remote <NAME>
          The remote the series come from [default: `upstream` when it exists, else `origin`]

      --addon <GLOB>
          Only the addons matching this glob

      --write-blacklist
          Blacklist the false positives (oca-port files) in commits on the branch `<to>-sweep`

      --open-pr
          Then push the branch and open a draft pull request

      --push-remote <NAME>
          With --open-pr: push to this remote instead of the target or your fork

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml to use (a repos.yaml for the commands that read one)

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve forge and index data from the cache only; a repository not in the cache yet is still fetched. Local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only
